  partName: Exhaust Manifold Right
  description: The Exhaust Manifold Right is a large, elongated metal component positioned
    at the middle-left-center of the engine, playing a crucial role in collecting
    and directing exhaust gases from the cylinders to the exhaust system. Made of
    metal-mid material, it is designed to handle high temperatures and pressures,
    and its location enables optimal exhaust gas flow. Notably, the Exhaust Manifold
    Right is slightly different from its left counterpart in terms of material, allowing
    for varying thermal expansion rates.
